<title>FRANCE: Total La Mede plant joins 24-hr French oil strike.</title>
<headline>Total La Mede plant joins 24-hr French oil strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Total's La Mede refinery joined a one-day protest over jobs at several French plants on Tuesday, union and company officials said</p>
<p>A spokesman for France's largest union, the CFDT, said 85 percent of shift workers had gone on strike from 1100 GMT, echoing similar action at Total's Gonfreville refinery.</p>
<p>The action at La Mede slowed the plant down, he said. Strikes at 130,000 barrels per day (bpd) La Mede and 210,000 bpd Gonfreville were intended for one day but renewable, he said.</p>
<p>A Total spokeswoman said there were strikers in both plants but there were no immediate details of the production impact.  </p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
